[h1]Replimat Mech[/h1]
[i]A fork of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1715402900]Replimat[/url] by Robin "sumghai" Chang and Dubwise56 and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3806650178]Replimat Universal[/url] by Omnot. Unofficial; not endorsed by the original authors.[/i]

A copier for your colony's production.
The matter splitter splits items and corpses into matter (mass and value) and records their patterns.
Replicators print from those patterns, paying time, mass and value.
A mechanitor sets up the print queues through a comms console.
Mechanoids are printed like in a gestator.
Nothing living is printed.

[b]Incompatible with Replimat and Replimat Universal.[/b]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/1.jpg[/img]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Matter splitter[/b]: splits what haulers bring into matter and records each pattern at the best quality seen. Corpses split like cremation, without mood penalties; a mech corpse gives its pattern if you can gestate that mech. It takes what its filter allows, like a stockpile; [b]Scan[/b] has one piece brought in past the filter.
[*][b]Replimat tanks[/b] store mass up to capacity and value without limit, shared across the network; the large one holds four times more.
[*][b]Replicators[/b] (standing and wall) print in batches of up to a stack. The [b]animal replicator[/b] prints feed into itself.
[*][b]Computer window[/b] from a comms console: [b]Home[/b], [b]Patterns[/b] (vanilla category tree, bill form), [b]Queue[/b] (all bills, edited in the row).
[*][b]Bills like vanilla[/b]: Do X times, Do until you have X, Do forever; first and second queue; pause; drag to reorder; move to another replicator.
[*][b]Sliders[/b]: print faster for more value or cheaper for more time, up to 40%.
[*][b]Print speed[/b] is the mechanitor's mech forming speed (crafting, gestation processors).
[*][b]Only researched things are printed[/b], like vanilla: buildings, recipes, crops, chips and techprints need their research; mined, wild and found things need none.
[*]Paid matter is never lost: deleting or moving a bill returns the unprinted batch.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/2.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/3.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/4.png[/img]

[h2]Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Research [b]Replication[/b] (after Microelectronics basics).
[*]Make an [b]isolinear module[/b] at a machining table.
[*]On one power network build a [b]replimat computer[/b], [b]replimat tanks[/b], a [b]matter splitter[/b] and a [b]replicator[/b].
[*]Allow items in the splitter's filter (all off by default) or use [b]Scan[/b].
[*]A mechanitor at a comms console: [b]Contact the replimat computer[/b], pick a pattern, create a bill.
[/olist]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/5.jpg[/img]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Mass and value collected on splitting (value 5–60%, so print-and-split never profits), color, print quality cap, special items (allow, markup), mechanitor required (off: no print speed or mechanoids), movable tanks, tank capacity, power use.
Stored value adds to colony wealth; [b]Collect value[/b] on the Home tab turns it off.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
RimWorld [b]1.6[/b]. Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url] and [b]Biotech[/b]. Languages: English, Russian.
Works with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2606448745]Multiplayer[/url]: edits are synced, the computer window opens only for the player who gave the order; mod settings must match the host.

